@startuml AD-7
!include _style.iuml
title AD-7 (System level) — Charge Point fault: report, alert, remote reset\nTrigger: a Driver fault report, a Faulted status, or an offline alert\nUse cases: UC-CHG-05, UC-INT-04, UC-OPS-03, UC-OPS-04, UC-OPS-08 [Should] · Rules: BR-P28, BR-P42

|«person»\nOperator|
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
|«external system»\nCharge Point|
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
start
:Receive fault signal (Driver report,\nFaulted status or offline alert)<
if ( ) then ([Driver report])
  :Record the report\nagainst the connector;
  :FaultReport]
  if ( ) then ([2nd Driver within 2 h, or\nconnector status abnormal])
    :Show "reported issue"\nlabel on the connector;
  else ([else])
    :Keep the report for\nlater grouping;
    stop
  endif
else ([Faulted status\nor offline alert])
endif
:Raise fault event, hide connector from\nsearch and suggestions, void its\nreservations (no fee), alert Operator>
:FaultEvent\n&#91;raised&#93;]
:Reservation\n&#91;voided&#93;]
|«person»\nOperator|
:Acknowledge the alert;
:FaultEvent\n&#91;acknowledged&#93;]
if ( ) then ([remote reset may fix it])
  :Choose soft or hard reset;
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
  :Send reset command>
  :FaultEvent\n&#91;resetting&#93;]
  |«external system»\nCharge Point|
  :Restart and report\nconnector status>
  |«person»\nOperator|
else ([needs a site visit])
endif
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
if ( ) then ([connector reports Available\nwithin the reset timeout])
else ([reset rejected, timed out or still\nfaulted, or site visit needed])
  |«person»\nOperator|
  if ( ) then ([maintenance tickets\nin use (Should)])
    :Create maintenance ticket;
    :MaintenanceTicket\n&#91;open&#93;]
    :Fix on site and\nclose the ticket;
    :MaintenanceTicket\n&#91;closed&#93;]
  else ([Must only])
    :Fix on site outside\nthe system;
  endif
  |«external system»\nCharge Point|
  :Report connector\nAvailable>
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
endif
:Resolve fault, show connector again\nand clear "reported issue" label;
:FaultEvent\n&#91;resolved&#93;]
stop
@enduml
